-- S346 SkyCairn, 2026-10-08: reading procedures for the 28 colleges whose program map host refuses (24) or never
-- reaches (4) the reader, through program_source_procedure_set (service role). Handoff 346 priority 4.
-- Each record names the routes tried: the mapper's 403 (probe run 37198225537) or the Los Rios hosts' 404, one web
-- search restricted to the college's own domain (2026-10-08), and the reads that followed where a page turned up
-- (college page read runs 37825341320 and 37826122000). Sam's sheet 50 card 5: a refused map counts as settled once
-- the college's procedure names the other routes tried, so each record carries a workaround.
-- Applied 2026-10-08 ~18:5xZ through execute_sql in two statements (15 first records, then 13 merges); every
-- result's was_md5 matched its guard, and the 15 first records' md5s equal this file's JSON byte for byte.
-- Read back: 31 of 32 published maps settled (Palo Verde, not read, is the one left); 34 of 118 colleges hold a
-- procedure; the history trigger filed 28 prior rows under this procedure_by.
-- 15 first records (guard 'none'); 13 merged into the live record (guard: the md5 read just before the write;
-- r.procedure || {...} keeps every key the record holds and appends to hosts, steps, workarounds, answers, nuances).
-- Rollback: for a first record, update program_source_registry set procedure = null, procedure_by = null,
--   procedure_at = null where college = '<college>'. For a merged record, restore the prior row the history
--   trigger filed: update program_source_registry r set procedure = h.old_row->'procedure',
--   procedure_by = h.old_row->>'procedure_by', procedure_at = (h.old_row->>'procedure_at')::timestamptz
--   from program_source_registry_history h where h.college = r.college and h.changed_by = '<this run's by>'.

